WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:06.760
There is not other arc in One Piece that has been&nbsp;
anticipated by fans as hard and as long as Elbaf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.080
the country with the strongest&nbsp;
warriors in the world, home of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.000
the Giants and territory of the Emperor Shanks.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.600
And so today, we are talking about everything that&nbsp;
could and should happen in this long awaited arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.880
starting from the things that are absolutely&nbsp;
100% going to happen like Usopp leading an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:31.520
army of giants or Luffy finally reuniting&nbsp;
with Shanks and moving to the most insane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:37.280
Elbaf theories ever conceived like how God Enel&nbsp;
is going to return to attack the Land of Giants.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.240
Since Dr. Vegapunk has given us the intel&nbsp;
that Jaguar D. Saul is alive and well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.280
hiding the remains of the Ohara library&nbsp;
on Elbaf, it’s almost guaranteed that it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:56.000
the Straw Hats’ next destination. Not to&nbsp;
mention this note from Oda at Jump Festa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.240
that all but says we’re getting some&nbsp;
giant sized One Piece action in 2024.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.160
During the Egghead Island arc, Oda treated fans&nbsp;
to a detour to check on what all of the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:13.920
Yonkou besides Luffy are up to. And most of them&nbsp;
have been spending their down time absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.360
obliterating Luffy’s supernova allies, Kid and&nbsp;
Law. When Eustass Kid threatened the weakling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.520
pirates that call Shanks their friend, the&nbsp;
superior Red-Haired pirate wiped out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:30.560
master of magnetism with just a single slash of&nbsp;
his sword. Our old friends from Little Garden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:36.960
Dorry and Brogy also wiped out Kid’s ship with&nbsp;
their signature technique Hakoku Sovereignty.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.600
But thanks to this cutaway to Shanks and the&nbsp;
Giant Pirates, we know that Luffy’s touchdown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:48.080
in Elbaf means a reunion with some old friends.&nbsp;
Usopp is sure to be excited to reunite with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.920
heroes Dorry and Brogy, who the crew hasn’t seen&nbsp;
since Little Garden in the Alabasta Saga. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.400
Usopp might also get to see his other giant&nbsp;
comrades like Oimo and Kashi who were guards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.320
at Enies Lobby until Usopp revealed that the&nbsp;
government had tricked them into service.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.480
And while we’re meeting all of these giants&nbsp;
again, maybe even Hajrudin will show up along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.840
with the rest of the Grand Fleet depending&nbsp;
on what kind of mortal threat emerges on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:21.120
land of Elbaf. And I’ll be talking about who&nbsp;
the big bad of Elbaf will be in just a bit.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.800
Of course, the reunion with the giants is&nbsp;
nothing compared to the reunion we’ve been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:33.800
waiting for since Chapter 1 of the series: that’s&nbsp;
right - Luffy will finally meet Shanks once again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:40.400
now that he’s become a powerful pirate,&nbsp;
a Yonkou in the same class as his mentor.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.720
How will this play out? Well, Luffy is&nbsp;
sure to shed tears just like he did when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:50.240
he met with Sabo again, however, we don’t&nbsp;
think the tears will come first. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.120
before Shanks gets to mutter much at all,&nbsp;
he’ll get a Gum Gum punch to the face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.080
with Luffy finally proving that his&nbsp;
punches are as strong as a pistol.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:07.240
But there’s no guarantee that the reunion&nbsp;
will be totally friendly - at the end of Wano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.400
Shanks declared that it’s finally time for&nbsp;
his crew to seek out the One Piece. We’re not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:18.160
sure how many road poneglyphs Shanks has already&nbsp;
claimed, but Luffy and the Straw Hats have three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:24.000
of them and it’s unlikely that Shanks has the ones&nbsp;
from Zou or Wano since those were well hidden by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.200
their respective people and only shared them with&nbsp;
the Straw Hats after they saved their countries.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.720
Does this mean that just like Kid got wrecked,&nbsp;
Luffy will also find himself at the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.560
Shanks’ sword? Will Shanks reveal his true colors&nbsp;
in order to get his hands on the poneglyphs? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.400
he probably doesn’t need to since he likely&nbsp;
retrieved all of the poneglyph etchings from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:51.200
what little remains of Kid’s crew. They did&nbsp;
offer them to him in order to try and save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.360
themselves, after all, just before their&nbsp;
ship was demolished by Dorry and Brogy.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.640
Speaking of which, we are going to have to&nbsp;
find out exactly what became of Eustass Kid.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:06.280
Luffy will probably be surprised to see that his&nbsp;
rival, who helped take out Big Mom and Kaidou,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:13.320
has been decimated by his old mentor. Of course,&nbsp;
we know how bad Oda is at killing off characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:19.800
so is Kid actually dead? Or will he show back up&nbsp;
on Elbaf with even more metal body parts - enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:24.920
that he could straight up be mistaken for a&nbsp;
Franky creation. Will he finally give up on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.720
trying to defeat Shanks, or will he crawl&nbsp;
his way back onto Elbaf only to give us a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:34.640
Shocked Enel face when he sees Luffy and&nbsp;
Shanks palling around eating giant hunks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:42.040
of meat together? And that’s only one of the Enel&nbsp;
faces we’ll get this arc…but more on that later.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:47.640
Shanks would make for a hell of a twist&nbsp;
villain. Just imagine&nbsp; Luffy’s mentor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:52.960
and hero who inspired him to become a pirate&nbsp;
from the very beginning ending up being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:58.840
ultimate obstacle preventing him from his&nbsp;
dream would be devastating. But as popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:05.480
as the Evil Shanks theory is…I just don’t see&nbsp;
it. He has an entire fleet of weakling pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:10.440
who he defends even though they’re not strong&nbsp;
enough to make it in the New World. He stopped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.520
the Marineford War to prevent further bloodshed.&nbsp;
He inspires young people like Luffy and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:26.720
young giant on Elbaf to become pirates. He just&nbsp;
doesn’t seem that evil, as mysterious as he is.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.600
Maybe we’ll even get an answer to some of the&nbsp;
mysteries that surround Shanks in this arc - is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:38.120
he a celestial dragon? Why was he found in a&nbsp;
treasure chest on God Valley? It only makes sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:43.080
that we’d get answers to these questions&nbsp;
and more in this Shanks -centered arc.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.720
However, Shanks doesn’t seem to&nbsp;
have a way to read the poneglyphs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:54.000
so maybe there’s another way besides force to&nbsp;
get something he needs. Instead of going all out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.320
in a battle against the Straw Hats, maybe we’ll&nbsp;
see a return to the Davy Back Fight. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:05.240
Long Ring Long Land is one of the few One&nbsp;
Piece arcs that doesn’t appear to have much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:10.360
foreshadowing or connection to other&nbsp;
arcs - which makes many One Piece fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:16.200
speculate that the Davy Back Fight will play&nbsp;
an important role at some point in the story.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:22.400
Just imagine a footrace between Sanji and&nbsp;
Lucky Roo, the supposed fastest character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:28.640
in the series. A musical matchup between Soul&nbsp;
King Brook and another rockstar…Rockstar - even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:33.520
though Bonk Punch is their actual musician.&nbsp;
And the ultimate game of darts between father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:40.320
and son when Usopp finally gets to show&nbsp;
Yasopp how much he’s grown as a marksman.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:48.600
Oh, and speaking of Usopp - if Whole Cake Island&nbsp;
gave us the year of Sanji and Wano gave Zoro a ton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:56.200
of focus…then welcome to the Year of Usopp.&nbsp;
No character has dreamed of visiting Elbaf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.200 --> 00:07:00.680
more than Usopp. He’s been the one to make&nbsp;
friends with all of the giants the crew has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:08.200
met along their journey. Well, except Hajrudin.&nbsp;
Hajrudin just started worshiping Usopp as a God.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.560
It’s just fitting that on this&nbsp;
island of brave, powerful warriors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.880
Usopp will also finally be able to&nbsp;
reunite with his father, Yasopp. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:23.040
this is sure to be the arc that Usopp finally&nbsp;
lives out his dream of becoming a Brave Warrior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:30.360
of the Sea. Most One Piece fans know that&nbsp;
Usopp’s lies have a tendency to come true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:36.520
which also means that in this arc it’s likely&nbsp;
that Usopp will lead an army of 8,000 men. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:44.840
not just any men - an army of giants. Who exactly&nbsp;
will this army be fighting? Only time will tell.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:52.760
Usopp is also due for a major powerup. And while I&nbsp;
can definitely see him using Vegapunk tech to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:59.080
the most technologically advanced slingshot of&nbsp;
all time, Elbaf will be the arc that Usopp taps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:04.520
into a new haki ability. He’s already had one&nbsp;
of the greatest observation Haki feats in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:09.600
series when he took out Sugar on Dressrosa from&nbsp;
super far away. But this might just be the arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:16.640
when he taps into Conqueror’s Haki. After all,&nbsp;
somebody fit to lead an entire army of 8,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.400
giants seems like the perfect candidate&nbsp;
to have the Color of the supreme King.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:29.920
Speaking of Conqueror’s Haki users, we might&nbsp;
just get the return of a former Yonkou:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:37.560
Big Mom, albeit with way more lava scars.&nbsp;
I already mentioned with Kid how bad Oda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:41.800
is with killing off characters,&nbsp;
so will Big Mom crawl her way out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:45.720
of the lava beneath Wano to seek revenge&nbsp;
against the Straw Hats and their allies?

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:53.160
Even if Big Mom is actually dead, she’ll be&nbsp;
sure to affect the Elbaf arc. Her flashback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:59.520
with Mother Carmel is the first time we actually&nbsp;
got to see Elbaf in the manga. It also felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.280
certain plot threads in Whole Cake Island&nbsp;
went unresolved with Big Mom seeking to ally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:09.880
with the giants and add Elbaf to her forces,&nbsp;
enabling her to finally claim the One Piece.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:16.160
We’re certain to meet Loki, the Prince of Giants,&nbsp;
who was arranged to marry Big Mom’s daughter Lola.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:20.160
Maybe while we’re at it, we’ll even get to&nbsp;
see Lola again as well as her twin sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:25.560
Chiffon along with Capone Bege and Pound. It’ll&nbsp;
be a bonafide Whole Cake Island reunion. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:30.520
we’re at it, if Blackbeard shows up as the&nbsp;
arc’s villain, it would make sense for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:36.320
remnants of the Big Mom pirates to face him&nbsp;
down since he’s kidnapped Pudding. Katakuri&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:41.600
and Luffy could join forces to make the&nbsp;
stretchiest team up in all of manga.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:47.120
And while I’m talking about Big Mom - will the&nbsp;
giants kind of recognize Zeus and freak out once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:53.880
Nami shows up on the island? Given their history&nbsp;
with Mother Carmel and Big Mom, a lot of them are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.880 --> 00:10:00.000
sure to recognize the concept of homies, and some&nbsp;
of them might even recognize Zeus specifically.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:08.560
And Zeus isn’t the only lightning user who we’re&nbsp;
bound to see on Elbaf. If there’s a Loki, we need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:16.000
a Thor and El Thor happens to be a signature&nbsp;
attack of the one and only God Enel. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:22.560
for anyone who’s been skipping their cover stories&nbsp;
- you’re missing out - because one cover story has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:29.760
confirmed that Enel survived Skypiea and ended up&nbsp;
flying his Arc Maxim all the way to Fairy Vearth:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:35.800
The Moon. That’s right - it’s time for Moon Piece.&nbsp;
On the moon, he found the remains of an advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:43.040
civilization and used his electricity to awaken a&nbsp;
literal robot army of automatons. Oh, also he met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:48.080
actual space pirates…There’s no way that all&nbsp;
of this doesn’t become relevant in the story.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:54.680
With the Final Saga well underway, we’re running&nbsp;
out of time to bring Enel back into the fold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.680 --> 00:11:00.440
so it’s only a matter of time before this wannabe&nbsp;
God shows back up. In fact, we’ll probably learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:07.720
a lot more about Sky Islanders in general: The Mad&nbsp;
Monk Urouge is the last supernova that has yet to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:14.320
play a pivotal role in one of the story arcs. It&nbsp;
just so happens that Urouge is also from Birka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:20.800
the same Sky Island that Enel destroyed before&nbsp;
moving on to Skypiea with his priests. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:26.680
very much possible that Urouge even used to be&nbsp;
one of Enel’s priests before they parted ways.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:31.800
Elbaf will likely treat us to more lore&nbsp;
about Sky Islands in general. When the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:35.600
Straw Hats went to Skypiea, the Sky&nbsp;
Islanders were shocked that they’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:39.640
used the Knock Up Stream to arrive there&nbsp;
since it’s an extremely dangerous route.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:45.680
They referenced that the more common&nbsp;
way to travel to Skypiea is by taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:54.680
something called the High West Road - could&nbsp;
this be connected to the Treasure Tree Adam?

00:11:54.680 --> 00:12:00.280
During Big Mom’s flashback, we see a giant&nbsp;
black mass rising completely perpendicular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:06.680
to the land. It’s so big we only get a sliver&nbsp;
of its total size from the panel. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:13.240
most fans speculate that this is actually&nbsp;
the Treasure Tree Adam - the legendary tree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:19.320
known for having the strongest wood in the&nbsp;
world, which the Thousand Sunny is made out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:25.080
of. Could climbing this tree be the secret&nbsp;
to reaching other Sky Islands? After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.600
the Giant Warriors of Elbaf are based on&nbsp;
Norse Mythology, which features the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:34.760
Tree Yggdrasil which stretches all the&nbsp;
way up to Asgard, the realm of the Gods.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:40.480
Of course, if the moon does become relevant&nbsp;
and the Straw Hats need to learn more about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:44.920
the ancient civilizations of the One&nbsp;
Piece world, they might need to go even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:52.000
higher than sky islands. Luckily, they have now&nbsp;
befriended the greatest scientist in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:58.080
and if anybody is capable of&nbsp;
space travel - it’s Dr. Vegapunk.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:03.840
Of course, the Moon is just the tip of the iceberg&nbsp;
when it comes to the wild lore reveals Oda’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:08.640
probably going to give us in Elbaf. In Egghead&nbsp;
Island, we learned that Robin’s favorite giant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:15.360
Jaguar D. Saul is alive and hiding on Elbaf. That&nbsp;
means it’s extremely likely that he’s uncovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:20.600
the secrets that the scholars of Ohara learned.&nbsp;
We might finally get to hear the words that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:26.040
Professor Clover was killed for threatening&nbsp;
to reveal: the name of the Ancient Kingdom.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:32.920
We’ll probably at least learn the location of&nbsp;
the Final Poneglyph and who could be guarding it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:39.440
if it’s not on Elbaf itself. Jaguar D.&nbsp;
Saul is one contender to be revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.960
as the man with the burn scars, since he&nbsp;
survived the burning of Ohara. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.360
since the Man with the Burn Scars is&nbsp;
supposed to be hiding on an all black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.960
ship surrounded by whirlpools, Saul&nbsp;
doesn’t quite fit the bill. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:57.040
Elbaf will likely give us a clue as to&nbsp;
where this mysterious figure can be found.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:01.880
Speaking of the Adam Tree, we might finally&nbsp;
learn more about the Treasure Tree Adam and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:09.680
its counterpart the Sunlight Tree Eve, which&nbsp;
grows in Mariejois. And what grows on trees?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:14.480
Fruits - like…devil fruits. So, while&nbsp;
we already got a lot of new information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:21.320
about devil fruits on Egghead, we might&nbsp;
learn even more of their secrets in Elbaf.

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:25.440
Along with the Norse mythology that’s&nbsp;
inspired characters like Shanks, Loki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:30.720
and the other Giants who take after Vikings,&nbsp;
maybe we’ll learn even more. All the way back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:34.680
in Little Garden, when Dorry and Brogy use&nbsp;
their Hakoku Sovereignty technique to defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:39.680
the Island Eater Fish, they mention that&nbsp;
the only thing their attack can’t pierce is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:46.560
the Serpent Soaked in Blood. Norse Mythology&nbsp;
features a creature called the Jormungandr:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:53.360
the giant snake that wraps around the entire&nbsp;
world. Hmmm…What’s something that wraps all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:58.680
the way around the One Piece world and is also&nbsp;
red-&nbsp; the color of something soaked in blood?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:05.920
That’s right - the Red Line itself. Maybe we’ll&nbsp;
even get to learn the history of this expansive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:12.720
geological structure - along with another winged&nbsp;
race of people who lived there: the Lunarians.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:20.480
Will we even see an apocalyptic war on the&nbsp;
level of the Norse Myth of Ragnarok? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:25.360
we’ve already seen weapons with apocalyptic&nbsp;
power in the series: the ancient weapons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:29.920
The three islands that have had the most&nbsp;
buildup in the series were Fishman Island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:35.040
Wano, and Elbaf. Fishman Island, which was first&nbsp;
mentioned during Arlong Park, ended up being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:40.360
hiding place of Poseidon, AKA Princess Shirahoshi.&nbsp;
Wano, which was first mentioned in Thriller Bark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:44.760
is the hiding place of the battleship&nbsp;
Pluton. So will Elbaf, which was first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:50.520
referenced all the way back in Little Garden,&nbsp;
be the place where we see Uranus in action.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:56.440
Since it’s likely that Uranus is the weapon&nbsp;
that was used by Imu to destroy Lulusia Kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:01.640
we may have already seen it - but Elbaf could be&nbsp;
the place where the World Government tries to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:07.760
it against the Straw Hats themselves. Of course,&nbsp;
that’s not the only possibility. Maybe the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:13.680
Uranus is whatever hatched from the giant egg&nbsp;
on the back of Roger’s ship, the Oro Jackson.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:20.880
Most important of all, though, is more lore about&nbsp;
Sun God Nika. Thanks to Mother Carmel during Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:27.320
Mom’s flashback, we already know that the giant of&nbsp;
Elbaf worship a Sun God. This means that Elbaf is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:32.640
the perfect place to learn more about the original&nbsp;
Sun God Nika and the original Joyboy and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:38.440
actions during the Void Century. In fact, since&nbsp;
Imu is guarding a giant Straw Hat within Pangea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:45.320
Castle, it’s likely that the original Joyboy was a&nbsp;
giant or at least a member of the Bucaneer Tribe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:50.720
like Bartholomew Kuma - and the person who’s&nbsp;
inherited his will has retained the same fashion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:56.280
sense. What better way to learn about this&nbsp;
ancient giant than from the giants of today?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:03.400
But even more than Lore Piece, what fans are&nbsp;
really craving from the Elbaf arc is some non-stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:08.840
giant sized action. We want to see battle axes&nbsp;
the size of buildings flying around and super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:14.840
sized conqueror’s haki clashes. So who will&nbsp;
be the ultimate villain of the Elbaf Arc?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:21.000
Will another Gorosei or even Imu-Sama descend on&nbsp;
the island after Saturn gets stomped on Egghead?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:26.200
That would be a good reason for Uranus to show&nbsp;
up as well as a good reason for the Straw Hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:30.160
to call on the help of the Grand Fleet.&nbsp;
After all, the world government has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:35.960
trying to use science to recreate giants for&nbsp;
ages - maybe this time they’ll come straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:40.240
to the source. Will God’s Knights leap&nbsp;
into action - resulting in Shanks having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:46.640
to reconcile with his past when his probable&nbsp;
father, Figarland Garling sets foot on Elbaf?

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:51.640
What if Prince Loki is unlike the rest&nbsp;
of the kindly giants we’ve met so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:56.480
and more like his trickster namesake from&nbsp;
Norse mythology? Maybe the Straw Hats will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.480 --> 00:18:00.480
actually find themselves at odds with the&nbsp;
Giant royalty. Or perhaps there will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:06.000
an even greater twist where someone we assume&nbsp;
is a friend is actually an antagonist and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.840
Evil Shanks theory will come true after&nbsp;
all. Maybe we’ll even get a completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:17.000
anti-climactic Enel rematch with him leading&nbsp;
a robot army against the Land of Giants.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:22.360
But more than all these, there’s one&nbsp;
villain more likely than any other:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:29.120
Blackbeard. Shanks has been a rival of&nbsp;
Blackbeard throughout the series. Teach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:33.720
gave him his signature scar across his eyes and&nbsp;
Shanks took the time to warn Whitebeard of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:39.160
threat the wielder of the darkness fruit posed. At&nbsp;
Marineford, Blackbeard stated that it wasn’t time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:45.720
for his crew to face Shanks…yet - which implies&nbsp;
the two will fight before the end of the series.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:49.920
Blackbeard could roll up to Elbaf in&nbsp;
search of the remaining poneglyph,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:55.440
either to steal whichever ones Shanks might have&nbsp;
or to gain clues from Jaguar D. Saul. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:59.080
Oda’s stated his primary hobby is archaeology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:04.000
so he’d love to get his hands on the remains&nbsp;
of Ohara’s library. As he approached,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:09.560
he’d lay waste to the weakling crews that are&nbsp;
allied with Shanks, succeeding where Kid failed.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:14.720
He’d have an epic matchup with Shanks,&nbsp;
making for one of the greatest duels in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:20.160
One Piece history. Shanks, the greatest&nbsp;
Haki master in the series vs. Blackbeard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:25.280
the only character to wield multiple devil&nbsp;
fruits. Perhaps we’ll even get the reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:30.400
of Blackbeard’s long-rumored third devil&nbsp;
fruit, which many fans think is a Cerberus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:35.280
or Kraken fruit - a mythical zoan to&nbsp;
go along with his logia and paramecia.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:41.320
The worst and most likely outcome of&nbsp;
this fight is that Shanks would lose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:46.600
before Luffy is able to arrive. Imagine the&nbsp;
heartbreak every One Piece fan would feel is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:51.200
Luffy was finally able to reunite with&nbsp;
Shanks and return the straw hat to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:55.760
only for Shanks to give dying words of&nbsp;
how proud he is of Luffy and leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.760 --> 00:20:00.120
the One Piece and the title of King of the&nbsp;
Pirates in the hands of the next generation.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:05.880
I absolutely don’t want this to happen&nbsp;
because Shanks dying at the hands of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:11.080
coward like Blackbeard would be criminal.&nbsp;
However, the resulting rage that Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:16.200
would fly into in facing down Blackbeard, who&nbsp;
was now responsible for the deaths of the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:22.000
most important people in his life, would be the&nbsp;
most intense scene in the entire series so far.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:27.400
Elbaf is sure to deliver one of the&nbsp;
craziest arcs in all of One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:32.360
finally letting us know more about the culture&nbsp;
of the giant race. Of course, there are still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:36.240
many people in One Piece we still need to&nbsp;
learn more about like the Lunarians and Sky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:42.800
Islanders. Here’s to hoping we get more answers&nbsp;
in Elbaf - but for now, you can get a reminder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:52.440
on everything we know so far by checking out&nbsp;
this video covering all of the One Piece races.

